# Checksum-verified data is checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# The shipping resolver gates its data load on a SHA-256 of the file's bytes
# (lib/shipping-resolver/data.ts), and its test fixtures are pinned to literal
# hashes. With git's core.autocrlf=true — the Windows default — checkout
# rewrites LF to CRLF, the bytes change, the hash no longer matches, the loader
# correctly refuses the file, and 11 resolver tests fail for a reason that has
# nothing to do with the code. Pinning eol keeps a checksum-verified artifact
# byte-identical wherever it is checked out.
#
# Deliberately scoped to the checksum-gated paths rather than all *.json, so
# this does not renormalize unrelated committed files.
lib/shipping-resolver/__tests__/fixtures/*.json text eol=lf
data/shipping-facts-*.json                      text eol=lf
